### Correct implementation

```java
public static int findSecondLargest(int[] arr) {
    int largest = arr[0];
    int secondLargest = 0;
    boolean foundSecondLargest = false;

    for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] > largest) {
            secondLargest = largest;
            largest = arr[i];
            foundSecondLargest = true;
        } else if (arr[i] < largest &&
                   (!foundSecondLargest || arr[i] > secondLargest)) {
            secondLargest = arr[i];
            foundSecondLargest = true;
        }
    }

    return foundSecondLargest ? secondLargest : arr[0];
}
```

This handles duplicates, all-equal arrays, negative numbers, and values equal to `Integer.MIN_VALUE`. It runs in **O(n)** time and uses **O(1)** extra space.

